WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.690 --> 00:00:07.089
Combining science-fiction action with crude
humor, a vast mythology, and just the tiniest

00:00:07.089 --> 00:00:12.749
bit of heart, Rick &amp; Morty was an instant
hit when it debuted on Adult Swim in late

00:00:12.749 --> 00:00:13.860
2013.

00:00:13.860 --> 00:00:19.960
The creation of animator and voice actor Justin
Roiland and Community creator Dan Harmon,

00:00:19.960 --> 00:00:25.460
the animated series follows the adventures
of a somewhat reprehensible, usually drunk

00:00:25.460 --> 00:00:31.750
scientist, and his kind of dumb grandson,
as they travel through space, time, and alternate

00:00:31.750 --> 00:00:36.510
dimensions messing up history, the universe,
and their own lives in the process.

00:00:36.510 --> 00:00:41.039
Here's a look at the untold truth of Rick
&amp; Morty.

00:00:41.039 --> 00:00:42.499
Doc and Mharti

00:00:42.499 --> 00:00:48.019
The whole thing started when Roiland made
an animated short called "The Real Animated

00:00:48.019 --> 00:00:54.719
Adventures of Doc and Mharti" : a very thinly
veiled, sexually-explicit parody of Back to

00:00:54.719 --> 00:00:55.719
the Future.

00:00:55.719 --> 00:00:58.589
If that sounds insane, that's because it is.

00:00:58.589 --> 00:00:59.629
"Great scott!"

00:00:59.629 --> 00:01:04.720
Roiland's cartoons were screened as part of
a weekly film showcase in Los Angeles run

00:01:04.720 --> 00:01:06.050
by Harmon.

00:01:06.050 --> 00:01:11.940
When Harmon got temporarily fired from Community,
he approached Roiland about adapting "Doc

00:01:11.940 --> 00:01:17.750
and Mharti" into a recurring series that toned
down some of the more explicit sexual content.

00:01:17.750 --> 00:01:22.710
Doc became Rick, Mharti became Morty, and
Bird Person became whatever he is.

00:01:22.710 --> 00:01:26.500
"It has been a challenging mating season for
Bird Person."

00:01:26.500 --> 00:01:28.690
"Then it's time to get your beak wet tonight,
playa!

00:01:28.690 --> 00:01:31.760
Have some fun out there, Bird Person."

00:01:31.760 --> 00:01:32.760
Gas giant

00:01:32.760 --> 00:01:35.040
"I have a new (BURP) catchphrase.

00:01:35.040 --> 00:01:36.580
I need your help, Morty.

00:01:36.580 --> 00:01:40.860
I mean we gotta get the hell out of here and
go take care of business.

00:01:40.960 --> 00:01:42.820
(BURP) (BURP) It's important.

00:01:42.820 --> 00:01:43.820
Come on Morty!"

00:01:43.820 --> 00:01:48.730
Rick's endless burping is definitely gross
— and it’s definitely real.

00:01:48.730 --> 00:01:53.850
Roiland, who voices both Rick and Morty, says
that during voiceover recording, he'll read

00:01:53.850 --> 00:01:58.560
through Rick's lines once, and mark down where
he wants to insert the burps later.

00:01:58.560 --> 00:02:03.750
With the help of a bunch of Miller 64 and
water, Roiland goes back and re-records his

00:02:03.750 --> 00:02:07.280
dialogue, this time with the belches in their
proper place.

00:02:07.280 --> 00:02:09.470
He says the "whole process is disgusting."

00:02:09.470 --> 00:02:13.910
"You can’t just add a sci-fi word to a car
word and hope it means something."

00:02:13.910 --> 00:02:17.160
That’s not the only all-natural part of
the process.

00:02:17.160 --> 00:02:22.030
The off-the-cuff feel to much of the dialogue
is because Roiland engages in a process of

00:02:22.030 --> 00:02:24.230
improvisation during recording.

00:02:24.230 --> 00:02:29.390
After running Rick's lines, Roiland does a
readthrough for Morty, and then does a take

00:02:29.390 --> 00:02:33.870
of the scene as both characters, letting himself
riff.

00:02:33.870 --> 00:02:39.730
The end result is a collage of scripted and
improvised lines that are animated around,

00:02:39.730 --> 00:02:46.070
resulting in some pretty amazingly weird,
and occasionally drunk, stuff.

00:02:46.070 --> 00:02:47.070
Instagram innovation

00:02:47.070 --> 00:02:52.650
Hundreds of shows have debuted on the internet,
but Rick &amp; Morty is the first to ever premiere

00:02:52.650 --> 00:02:55.240
an entire episode on Instagram.

00:02:55.240 --> 00:03:01.850
Due to Instagram's video limitation of 15
seconds, that meant the 2014 episode, “Rixty

00:03:01.850 --> 00:03:05.780
Minutes,” had to be cut up into 109 separate
videos.

00:03:05.780 --> 00:03:11.650
Building on its unique success, the show team
also did something else nobody had done on

00:03:11.650 --> 00:03:15.520
Instagram before: use it as a game platform.

00:03:15.520 --> 00:03:19.590
Rickstaverse launched in the summer of 2015.

00:03:19.590 --> 00:03:24.959
Players must follow tags and other clues to
bounce through more than 80 Instagram accounts

00:03:24.959 --> 00:03:28.270
set up and dedicated exclusively to the game.

00:03:28.270 --> 00:03:35.430
More than 129,000 people took part in Rickstaverse,
which involved 11 explorable planets and more

00:03:35.430 --> 00:03:39.810
than 1,000 individual images, and tied into
the Season Two cliffhanger.

00:03:39.810 --> 00:03:45.130
It even offered players the opportunity to
contribute to Season Three by naming a weird

00:03:45.130 --> 00:03:46.820
alien blob.

00:03:46.820 --> 00:03:47.820
The Couch Gag

00:03:50.400 --> 00:03:51.820
"Oh my god, did you do?

00:03:51.880 --> 00:03:54.500
You killed The Simpsons, Morty!"

00:03:54.510 --> 00:03:56.750
"I didn't mean to!"

00:03:56.820 --> 00:03:58.060
"Oh god look at the baby one!

00:03:58.060 --> 00:03:59.960
Oh my god Morty!"

00:03:59.960 --> 00:04:04.360
In 2016, the Rick &amp; Morty team put together
one of the most memorable Simpsons "couch

00:04:04.370 --> 00:04:06.510
gags" in recent memory.

00:04:06.510 --> 00:04:12.540
Justin Roiland had heard that Simpsons creator
Matt Groening was a fan of his show, so he

00:04:12.540 --> 00:04:17.739
asked Groening to provide the commentary track
on the DVD release of the first season of

00:04:17.739 --> 00:04:19.000
Rick &amp; Morty.

00:04:19.000 --> 00:04:24.910
Groening agreed, and brought along longtime
Simpsons writer and producer Al Jean, who

00:04:24.910 --> 00:04:30.850
asked Roiland to do the time-traveling couch
bit, and surprisingly, allowing him to brutally

00:04:30.850 --> 00:04:32.940
murder Springfield’s first family.

00:04:32.940 --> 00:04:38.160
Not only that, but the couch gag also doubled
as a Futurama crossover.

00:04:38.160 --> 00:04:43.660
And given the fact that Rick and Morty takes
place in a vast multi-verse, it’s not surprising

00:04:43.660 --> 00:04:47.570
that this isn’t the show’s only crossover.

00:04:47.570 --> 00:04:48.830
Gravity Falls

00:04:48.830 --> 00:04:53.470
Though they come from very different places
and have very different audiences, the connections

00:04:53.470 --> 00:04:57.660
between Gravity Falls and Rick and Morty are
too plentiful to ignore.

00:04:57.660 --> 00:05:03.030
Gravity Falls creator Alex Hirsch has done
voice work on Rick and Morty, and Roiland

00:05:03.030 --> 00:05:05.340
has returned the favor on Hirsch's show.

00:05:05.680 --> 00:05:06.700
"That’s amazing.

00:05:06.720 --> 00:05:09.220
Are you from the future or something?"

00:05:09.740 --> 00:05:10.300
"Uh no!

00:05:10.460 --> 00:05:11.700
Who told you that!

00:05:12.160 --> 00:05:13.360
Memory wipe!"

00:05:14.040 --> 00:05:15.840
"This is a baby wipe."

00:05:15.840 --> 00:05:20.419
Not too surprising, since they used to share
an office at the Disney Channel.

00:05:20.419 --> 00:05:22.040
But it goes deeper.

00:05:22.040 --> 00:05:28.510
For example, Gravity Falls' evil, pyramid-shaped
dream demon Bill Cipher briefly appeared in

00:05:28.510 --> 00:05:29.630
Rick &amp; Morty.

00:05:29.630 --> 00:05:33.510
As Hirsch told Entertainment Weekly, it’s
a dream come true, saying.

00:05:33.510 --> 00:05:38.730
“For some reason, the universe has blessed
us with our mad wishes, and it occurred to

00:05:38.730 --> 00:05:44.120
us — let's start doing things nobody else
does, that maybe you're not supposed to do.

00:05:44.120 --> 00:05:48.560
We started putting little Easter eggs in our
shows that sort of connected the two.

00:05:48.560 --> 00:05:54.160
Our motivation for that is primarily to freak
people out and blow their minds."

00:05:54.160 --> 00:06:00.090
One of the most mind-blowing Easter eggs occurs
when, spoiler alert, items sucked into a portal

00:06:00.090 --> 00:06:04.660
in Gravity Falls pop out through a portal
in Rick and Morty.

00:06:04.660 --> 00:06:06.470
Rick's a mystery

00:06:06.470 --> 00:06:11.919
As vast and complicated as the Rick &amp; Morty
mythos has become, Roiland and Harmon never

00:06:11.919 --> 00:06:15.810
want to give too much information about the
history of Rick.

00:06:15.810 --> 00:06:17.320
Harmon told The AV Club,

00:06:17.320 --> 00:06:22.130
"...we're very careful about delving into
Rick's backstory, because when we do, we don't

00:06:22.130 --> 00:06:25.150
want there to be any shocking surprises."

00:06:25.150 --> 00:06:31.220
Like Yoda and Tommy Wiseau, Rick’s real
story may never be revealed, and that’s

00:06:31.220 --> 00:06:34.690
just one of the show’s many mysteries.

00:06:34.690 --> 00:06:36.470
The plot thickens

00:06:36.470 --> 00:06:41.400
The show's creative staff decided they wanted
to have a "secret" about the show's world

00:06:41.400 --> 00:06:43.520
that only they would know.

00:06:43.520 --> 00:06:48.889
They would never explicitly reveal their secret
during the run of Rick &amp; Morty, but they did

00:06:48.889 --> 00:06:51.270
want to place clues throughout.

00:06:51.270 --> 00:06:56.250
Because fans are weirdly obsessive, someone
managed to figure out the secret and posted

00:06:56.250 --> 00:06:57.330
it on Reddit.

00:06:57.330 --> 00:07:02.289
Roiland confirmed that someone figured it
out, but didn't identify the secret.

00:07:02.289 --> 00:07:07.150
Based on the posts related to these theories
and Roiland's reaction, fans have narrowed

00:07:07.150 --> 00:07:09.690
it down the most likely possibilities.

00:07:09.690 --> 00:07:12.180
Could Rick be an older version of Morty?

00:07:12.180 --> 00:07:14.990
Or is he one of the many versions of Morty?

00:07:14.990 --> 00:07:17.320
Is Rick is aware that he’s a fictional character?

00:07:17.320 --> 00:07:19.370
"See you next week, everybody!"

00:07:19.370 --> 00:07:24.780
Or maybe Rick's flask isn't filled with booze,
but instead the powerful "mega seeds."

00:07:24.780 --> 00:07:27.380
"You gotta put these seeds inside your butt."

00:07:27.380 --> 00:07:28.440
"In my butt?"

00:07:28.580 --> 00:07:29.980
"Come on Morty—please Morty!

00:07:30.000 --> 00:07:31.180
You have to do it Morty!"

00:07:31.280 --> 00:07:31.960
"Oh man…"

00:07:32.280 --> 00:07:36.880
You know, the ones that temporarily make you
smart, but then kinda cripple you for a while?

00:07:36.980 --> 00:07:38.160
"Oh geez."

00:07:38.200 --> 00:07:39.820
"I'm sorry Morty, it's a bummer.

00:07:40.180 --> 00:07:42.800
In reality you're as dumb as they come."

00:07:42.800 --> 00:07:48.430
But the most important question of all: will
there ever be another season of Community?

00:07:48.430 --> 00:07:49.430
"Never."

00:07:49.430 --> 00:07:50.430
"Never!"

00:07:50.430 --> 00:07:51.430
Thanks for watching!

00:07:51.430 --> 00:07:53.940
Click the Looper icon to subscribe to our
YouTube channel.

00:07:53.940 --> 00:07:56.880
Plus check out all this cool stuff we know
you'll love, too!

